From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 15:30:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: sunxi: sun55i-pck600: Read the domain state at
 probe

The driver registers every domain as powered, whatever the PPU
reports. A domain that the boot firmware left off is then never
powered on for its first consumer: genpd takes it for on, skips
power_on(), and the consumer's first access goes to an unpowered
block. Whether that happens depends on the boot firmware.

Read the power status from PWSR and pass it to pm_genpd_init(). A
domain that reads on is held until the provider's sync_state() as
before; a domain that reads off is powered on when a consumer needs
it. Domains flagged always-on keep their declared state, as genpd
refuses an always-on domain that is registered off.

Not covered: the always-on flag of the A733 GPU_CORE domain.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; every domain the boot
chain left on is reported on, and each reported state matches the
domain's power state register.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/pmdomain/sunxi/sun55i-pck600.c | 19 ++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/sunxi/sun55i-pck600.c b/drivers/pmdomain/sunxi/sun55i-pck600.c
index 6d34101794d1..72b5cb79d358 100644
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/sunxi/sun55i-pck600.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/sunxi/sun55i-pck600.c
@@ -114,6 +114,13 @@ static int sunxi_pck600_power_off(struct generic_pm_domain *domain)
 	return sunxi_pck600_pd_set_power(pd, false);
 }
 
+static bool sunxi_pck600_pd_is_on(struct sunxi_pck600_pd *pd)
+{
+	u32 reg = readl(pd->base + PPU_PWSR);
+
+	return FIELD_GET(PPU_PWR_STATUS, reg) == PPU_POWER_MODE_ON;
+}
+
 static void sunxi_pck600_pd_setup(struct sunxi_pck600_pd *pd,
 				  const struct sunxi_pck600_desc *desc)
 {
@@ -170,6 +177,7 @@ static int sunxi_pck600_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	for (i = 0; i < desc->num_domains; i++) {
 		struct sunxi_pck600_pd *pd = &pck->pds[i];
 		const struct sunxi_pck600_pd_desc *pd_desc = &desc->pd_descs[i];
+		bool is_off;
 
 		pd->genpd.name = pd_desc->name;
 		pd->genpd.power_off = sunxi_pck600_power_off;
@@ -179,7 +187,16 @@ static int sunxi_pck600_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		pd->pck = pck;
 
 		sunxi_pck600_pd_setup(pd, desc);
-		ret = pm_genpd_init(&pd->genpd, NULL, false);
+
+		/*
+		 * Register each domain in the state the PPU reports, so that
+		 * a domain the boot firmware left off is powered on for its
+		 * first consumer. Always-on domains keep their declared state.
+		 */
+		is_off = !(pd->genpd.flags & GENPD_FLAG_ALWAYS_ON) &&
+			 !sunxi_pck600_pd_is_on(pd);
+
+		ret = pm_genpd_init(&pd->genpd, NULL, is_off);
 		if (ret) {
 			dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "failed to initialize power domain\n");
 			goto err_remove_pds;
